{"term":"admit","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:00d14ec4fefcca88f7","definition":"To allow to enter; to grant entrance (to), whether into a place, into the mind, or into consideration.","example":"to admit a serious thought into the mind","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["admit defeat","admittable","admittance","admittedly","admittee","admitter","admitting","admittingly","coadmit","nonadmitted","preadmit","re-admit","readmit","unadmittable","unadmitted","unadmittedly","unadmitting"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:43aa919ba93d27f551","definition":"To allow (someone) to enter a profession or to enjoy a privilege; to recognize as qualified for a franchise.","example":"to admit an attorney to practice law","pos":"verb","synonyms":["inlet","let in"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["admit defeat","admittable","admittance","admittedly","admittee","admitter","admitting","admittingly","coadmit","nonadmitted","preadmit","re-admit","readmit","unadmittable","unadmitted","unadmittedly","unadmitting"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/admit#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e5caa7fb2a9ae10cc","definition":"To concede as true; to acknowledge or assent to, as an allegation which it is impossible to deny (+ to).","example":"the argument or fact is admitted","pos":"verb","synonyms":["own up","confess","allow","acknowledge","own","grant"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["admit defeat","admittable","admittance","admittedly","admittee","admitter","admitting","admittingly","coadmit","nonadmitted","preadmit","re-admit","readmit","unadmitt